{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "00YG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0002": "$p, p'$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}$", "MATH_0004": "$u, u' : \\mathcal{C} \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0005": "$f : p \\to p'$", "MATH_0006": "$$\nf_u : u' \\to u.\n$$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-morphism-points}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:76ab084bb7ef483a43c494d9d2d302aa635a23ec7fa42a7eabbf019426b98a59", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:eea4b9ac6a927d4a85c5d57436b072ca0b3c2689a504b90ed5609ef600f3604e", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a site. Let <MATH_0002> be points of <MATH_0003>\ngiven by functors <MATH_0004>.\nA <TEXTITOPEN_0001>morphism <MATH_0005><TEXTITCLOSE_0001> is given by a transformation of\nfunctors\n<MATH_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:434e9ee7cb37f2bf73ca6cbed867713b7799a81e4649e67135da59a61b31eafd", "unit_id": "tag:00YI:statement"}
{"chapter": "sites", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "00YG", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$2$", "MATH_0003": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n\\textit{Sets}\n=\n\\Sh(pt)\n\\rrtwocell^p_{p'}{f}\n&\n&\n\\Sh(\\mathcal{C})\n}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$f_u$", "MATH_0005": "$p_* \\to p'_*$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{T}_G$", "MATH_0007": "$\\Mor(p, p')$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Mor(p_*, p'_*)$", "MATH_0009": "$x' \\in \\overline{\\{x\\}}$", "MATH_0010": "$X$", "MATH_0011": "$p \\to p'$", "MATH_0012": "$p$", "MATH_0013": "$p'$", "MATH_0014": "$X_{Zar}$", "MATH_0015": "$x$", "MATH_0016": "$x'$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-point-G-sets}", "SPACE_0001": "\\ ", "SPACE_0002": "\\ ", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0002": "\\medskip", "STRUCT_0003": "\\noindent", "STRUCT_0004": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\item", "STRUCT_0007": "\\item", "STRUCT_0008": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:2b5fd0363381f5852c5b655d1febe900c3e9ab5b96fb8748fd97443234c138c7", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4422bd7b8eabd82dc8e53807c8cd2b798757d67d540bdca52037ccd3db3743b5", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote how the transformation of functors goes the other way.\nThis makes sense, as we will see later, by thinking of\nthe morphism <MATH_0001> as a kind of <MATH_0002>-arrow pictorially as\nfollows:\n<MATH_0003>\nNamely, we will see later that <MATH_0004> induces a canonical\ntransformation of functors <MATH_0005> between\nthe skyscraper sheaf constructions.\n\n<STRUCT_0002><STRUCT_0003>\nThis is a fairly important notion, and deserves a more complete\ntreatment here. List of desiderata\n<STRUCT_0004>\n<STRUCT_0005> Describe the automorphisms of the point of <MATH_0006>\ndescribed in Example <REF_0001>.\n<STRUCT_0006> Describe <MATH_0007> in terms of  <MATH_0008>.\n<STRUCT_0007> Specialization of points in topological spaces.\nShow that if <MATH_0009> in the topological space\n<MATH_0010>, then there is a morphism <MATH_0011>, where <MATH_0012> (resp.<SPACE_0001><MATH_0013>)\nis the point of <MATH_0014> associated to <MATH_0015> (resp.<SPACE_0002><MATH_0016>).\n<STRUCT_0008>\n\n\n\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:1d72feffc389f7060ddff8bd7b81aca6d5be445f49c098065e6564cfd6a3f3d1", "unit_id": "tag:00YG:prose-0001"}
